  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-mobile-bnpl-image-plus-text (npm)",
  "details": "The package's main entry (index.js) loads a bundled dropper (_vendor.js) on require. The dropper downloads a platform-specific binary payload over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, and /pkg/package.exe, with a DNS TXT-record fallback channel using domains sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, and net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded payload is written to /tmp (or %TEMP% on Windows) under a random name (.cache_\u003chex\u003e or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"\u003cpath\u003e \u0026\" on Unix). A timestamp marker file suppresses re-execution for a few hours.",
